{
  "_doc": [
    "Which model runs each LLM step, across both pipelines. One place to change it (later: the studio UI's model page).",
    "Loaded by runtime/flows/shared/model_routing.py and personas/flows/shared/model_routing.py (identical copies).",
    "steps.*: model (must be listed under models), thinking ('adaptive' | 'off', Anthropic only), effort (null = don't send; model default).",
    "The loader refuses unsafe combinations: thinking 'off' on a model that can't disable it, or effort null on a model whose default isn't 'high' (a silent quality drop).",
    "Legacy per-step env vars (docs/LLM_CALL_INVENTORY.md §5) still override this file so existing run commands keep working; prefer editing here.",
    "Switching a voice-writing step's model changes how the voices write: re-validate the voices (sentinel regen) before relying on it. See runtime/OPEN_ITEMS.md C62.",
    "steps with \"manual\": true are done by the operator in claude.ai (no API call): the model is rendered into the instructions they paste, by its display_name; the API safety rules don't apply to them. See voices/OPEN_ITEMS.md §36.",
    "\"manual\": true is refused on any step key that doesn't start with \"personas.dr_\" — that's the only family of steps done by the operator instead of an API call; a config slip marking a real call site manual would otherwise skip the safety rules above (runtime/OPEN_ITEMS.md C67 #5)."
  ],

